Derived from BDI literature 
Agents are those entities in drama, that potentially 
-  have goals (object property hasGoal);
-  intend plans to achieve goals (op intends)
-  participate in actions with some role (op filler);

If some Agent (e.g. Polonius) is involved in an action without being intentional (e.g., being the topic of a conversation), it remains classified as an Agent in Drammar, though it fills a different role in the frame (e.g., Topic of Conversation).

Boolean property:
- true, if the value is at stake; 
- false, if the value is balanced.
